{
  "title": "Calorie estimates: ginger and turmeric pieces, knobs and chunks",
  "description": "17 Unsupported quantity unit lines (15 pipeline fixtures, 1 Paprika, 1 snapshot) are pieces of ginger or turmeric sized somewhere the weigher doesn't look. ginger root, raw already has inch-piece weights (\"1 inch piece\" 7.4 g, \"2 inch piece\" 14.8 g, …), and \"1 2-inch piece ginger\" already weighs. \
Failing shapes: the size in the note (\"1 piece fresh ginger\" noted \"2-inch-long\" / \"1 1/2 inches, peeled\" / \"approx 1/2 inch\"; 4 lines plus \"1 piece peeled ginger\" noted 2\"); the unit left in the item (\"1 inch knob fresh ginger\", \"0.5 inch ginger\", \"one-and-a-half inch chunk ginger\" with a spelled-out size, \"2 piece 1-inch fresh ginger root\"); a size word with no inches (\"1 small piece fresh ginger\", \"1 small knob ginger\"; treat as a cited 1-inch piece or leave unknown); and \"1 2-inch piece turmeric\" (turmeric root has no piece weights; needs a cited one). \
Fix in ingredient_parser/quantity.rs next to leading_size/named_piece: read an inch size from the note of a piece/knob/chunk count, and from an item that starts with \"inch knob|chunk|piece\". \
Measure with make ingredient-catalog-audit (Unsupported quantity unit, all three corpora) and, once blocked-ingredient-burndown-from-prod lands, the prod report; make pipeline should produce only data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md and fixture-category diffs. \
Server-side only (ramekin-core nutrition), so no web or iOS change. \
Split out of the retired p3-nutrition-remaining-count-units (owner, 2026-10-24: whole groups per PR, never one ingredient).",
